{"version":1,"entries":{"Children: Today is our school party. Let's go to the cafeteria and get the ice cream you bought yesterday. It's in the freezer. Oh no, it's liquid. Yuck. That was our ice cream.\n\nStudent A: Was the freezer door open?\n\nStudent B: Yes, it was. It was open all night. Now there's no ice cream for the party.\n\nMr. Jenkins: What's wrong? Why is everyone so sad?\n\nChildren: It was our job to bring the ice cream for the party, but it melted. Now we can't have ice cream.\n\nMr. Jenkins: Sure you can. You can make ice cream. I can teach you.\n\nChildren: Yippee.\n\nMr. Jenkins: Okay kids, get big and small plastic bags, cream, sugar, vanilla, and salt. Then come to my classroom.\n\nChildren: Ready, Mr. Jenkins?\n\nMr. Jenkins: My freezer was closed all night, so I have ice. Now let's make ice cream.\n\nChildren: Yes, let's make ice cream.\n\nMr. Jenkins: Mix the sugar and vanilla and cream.\n\nChildren: Mix the sugar and vanilla and cream, done.\n\nMr. Jenkins: Pour the cream, sugar, and vanilla mixture into the small bag.\n\nChildren: Pour the cream, sugar, and vanilla mixture into the small bag, done.\n\nMr. Jenkins: Put the salt and the ice cubes into the big bag.\n\nChildren: Put the salt and the ice cubes into the big bag, done.\n\nMr. Jenkins: Now put the small bag in the big bag.\n\nChildren: Put the small bag in the big bag, done.\n\nMr. Jenkins: Now shake, shake, shake. What do you have?\n\nChildren: Hey, look, we have ice cream and we didn't use a freezer. How is the ice cream, Mr. Jenkins?\n\nMr. Jenkins: It's great, can I have some more?":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/5285a03c85985271bc10.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/200b333eb9d0d3d01109.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Student A"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/9a21c5430e9558fe3be8.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Student B"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/32c2f342a12006312885.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/b4aa7d205e3567a9b8c0.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/5c5075ea6f6e38846573.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/b785acc2c4d783c60069.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/aa68dbf2cc46d774b048.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/467318ab2b05eb51cc17.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/25916f9fee6e178d6edf.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/0b6ad647104a0d250454.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/3d502429bc119de684b9.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/471c0e3455c8a9f0cf6b.mp3","turn":12,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/5eb4019d9b92f55a68d8.mp3","turn":13,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/4b291d8e85381c7bf621.mp3","turn":14,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/30865342faa40ff924d0.mp3","turn":15,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/29927174461573840456.mp3","turn":16,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/3bf26fb648f02818d3d7.mp3","turn":17,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/23fb83e607878133d175.mp3","turn":18,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/2e9ad4cb8d16be1d37d8.mp3","turn":19,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/1ff8e1fddba8712945b0.mp3","turn":20,"speaker":"Children"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/56b0e512125451fde049.mp3","turn":21,"speaker":"Mr. Jenkins"}],"Grandpa: Okay, says Grandpa. I'll tell you a story about my grandfather, Carlo. In 1910, Carlo was ten years old. He and his family lived in Italy. They were very poor, so they came to the United States for a better life. This was the first time that Carlo traveled to a place far away.\n\nHenry: Really? I'm ten, too, says Henry. And mom, dad, and I visit a different country every summer.\n\nGrandpa: Yes, Henry, things are different now, says Grandpa.\n\nHenry: How did they travel here, asks Henry?\n\nGrandpa: They traveled by ship, says Grandpa. It wasn't an easy trip, because the ship was crowded and dirty. There wasn't much food, and many people got sick. Carlo was sick, too. They arrived at Ellis Island in New York after ten days.\n\nHenry: Wow, that's slow, says Henry. Now it only takes about nine hours in an airplane.\n\nGrandpa: I know, says Grandpa. It's very different today.\n\nHenry: What happened at Ellis Island, asks Henry?\n\nGrandpa: Doctors checked everyone, and Carlo was very scared, says Grandpa.\n\nHenry: Why was he scared, Grandpa? Doctors help people, says Henry.\n\nGrandpa: Yes, but people who weren't healthy couldn't enter New York, says Grandpa. The clerks asked them many questions.\n\nHenry: What questions, Grandpa, asks Henry.\n\nGrandpa: Where are you from? Are you healthy or are you sick, says Grandpa? Luckily, Carlo was feeling better, so they let him in. And that's why we live here today and not in Italy.\n\nHenry: That was a cool story, Grandpa, says Henry. I have an idea. Let's take a trip to Italy.\n\nGrandpa: That's a good idea, Henry, says Grandpa. Let's go next summer.\n\nHenry: Awesome, Grandpa, but let's take an airplane, not a ship.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/e739c1d1077ed32267cf.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Grandpa"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/f2d4ac1fc70cb23ac277.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Henry"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/8e04907eef1160b08bbd.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Grandpa"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/ad141bee24a7753926d6.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Henry"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/676d6d99f414971621ca.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Grandpa"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/73fca206b89f997105ba.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Henry"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/ce910fa2bfc9eb073e53.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Grandpa"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/6132400895726f605d1a.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Henry"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/647a60a1980dfa3092e6.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Grandpa"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/ddb270e96928b23a1643.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Henry"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/ac49453203975bfc929c.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Grandpa"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/4c90ac64f94f30f71c67.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Henry"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/e162ad4901e40c92750d.mp3","turn":12,"speaker":"Grandpa"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/f7deb407bd37c88e0462.mp3","turn":13,"speaker":"Henry"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/c8be61be159ab12aebd7.mp3","turn":14,"speaker":"Grandpa"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/f18e5bd01d0b402ed81c.mp3","turn":15,"speaker":"Henry"}],"Narrator: A monkey called Bandar lived in the woods near a small town. One day Bandar was bored and decided to go into the town. Bandar went to a bakery and saw thirty beautiful cookies. He stole a cookie and ate it. It was good. He ate more and more cookies. The baker saw Bandar and chased him.\n\nBaker: You greedy little monkey! he cried. Now there are only fifteen cookies!\n\nNarrator: Bandar ran up a tree and hid in the leaves. When he looked down, he saw sixty small carrots in a garden. When the gardener wasn't looking, Bandar ran down the tree, dug up a carrot and ate it. It was good. He ate more and more carrots. The gardener saw Bandar and chased him.\n\nGardener: You greedy little monkey! Now there are only forty-four carrots!\n\nNarrator: Bandar went to a restaurant and saw forty-two sausages. He stole a sausage and ate it. It was good. He ate more and more sausages. The cook saw Bandar and chased him.\n\nCook: You greedy little monkey! Now there are only thirty sausages!\n\nNarrator: Bandar stole food all over town. Everyone was angry. They tried to catch Bandar, but he was too fast. Then the candy maker had an idea. The next day, Bandar went to the candy store. He saw two big jars of candy in every color, and it all looked good. Bandar put his hands in the jars and grabbed twenty pieces of candy. But he couldn't get the candy out of the jars. The candy maker ran in.\n\nCandy maker: You greedy little monkey! Let go of the candy and you can run away!\n\nNarrator: So did Bandar let go of the candy? No, he didn't, and the candy maker caught him. He took him back to the woods and told him never to come to town again.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/a0843b5c5f75decbd840.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/4c0411446c1c465dd053.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Baker"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/61fd83be43ab8d2aad81.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/bae451b618361391a7dc.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Gardener"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/e430db2e890508d022e3.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/8c69edc654bec117255e.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Cook"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/e2c2d61ddcaf03a5b2d9.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/ce971c3cc712b7196abb.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Candy maker"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/f7690532a65f6256d879.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Narrator"}],"Recycled carton (diary): January 15th. Dear Diary, I'm sitting on a shelf in a big store. I can see many wonderful things. The little carton in front of me has a picture of an orange on it. I think I know what I am. I'm an orange juice carton. I'm made of hard paper. January 16th. Dear Diary, this morning something great happened. A little girl looked at my shelf for a long time, and then she chose me. She's taking me to a picnic by the lake. So I hope she's very thirsty. January 17th. Dear Diary, I'm in a lake. The little girl drank the juice, but she left me in front of the lake. The wind blew me into the water. I don't like it here. There was a trash can behind the tree. Why didn't the little girl put me in it? January 18th. Dear Diary, I saw a man taking litter out of the lake with a net. He saw my bright orange carton and he rescued me. He caught me and a plastic bottle in his net. Now we're in the boat, and we aren't trash anymore. We're happy. January 19th. Dear Diary, I'm at the recycling plant. It's a little scary here because there are large machines that make loud noises. Where's my plastic bottle friend? He's across from me. He's in a bin with other plastic bottles. January 20th. Dear Diary, I'm sitting on a shelf in a stationery store. Everything here is made of paper. Yes, they recycled me into a notebook. I'm very happy and excited, and I really want to see the recycling plant again. Maybe next time, I'll be a comic book.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/93169eededacb83975bd.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Recycled carton (diary)"}],"Narrator: When Olga plays her flute, she feels many things. High and slow notes make her feel happy, and the low, long notes can make her feel sleepy. When Olga plays a fast tune, she feels like she is flying. Olga’s school is having a big concert tonight. Olga plays second flute, so if the first flute player gets sick, Olga can play his or her part. Today, Olga goes to school early for extra practice. Her music teacher is waiting for her.\n\nMr. Perez: Alonzo has the flu. You must play his part tonight.\n\nNarrator: Olga is very worried.\n\nOlga: Alonzo is the best flute player in the school. I'm not good enough.\n\nNarrator: Mr. Perez smiles.\n\nMr. Perez: You practice every day, Olga. Alonzo plays well, but so do you. Please try, Olga.\n\nNarrator: She closes her eyes and begins to play, but this morning she feels nervous. The high notes are hard to reach, and the fast notes are difficult to play. The quiet part seems too loud. When Olga finishes, her eyes fill with tears.\n\nOlga: I wish I could play like Alonzo.\n\nNarrator: Mr. Perez pushes a button on his computer, and Olga hears music. She thinks it is Alonzo’s flute solo. She imagines butterflies on the high notes. The fast notes sound like hummingbirds or rain. The low, quiet notes are like snow falling.\n\nOlga: That's beautiful. I wish I played like that.\n\nMr. Perez: Olga, I recorded you just now. That's you playing.\n\nNarrator: Olga is amazed.\n\nOlga: Do I really sound like that?\n\nNarrator: Mr. Perez laughs.\n\nMr. Perez: You should listen when you play.\n\nOlga: I do listen, but I'm often too nervous.\n\nMr. Perez: Don't worry tonight. You work hard and you play well, but never forget to have fun and enjoy the music. You're a great musician.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/4bc6cb11a0eb3fae6008.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/a42150700843b66586db.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Mr. Perez"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/e9a398527e8e18fcb308.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/a8ae1e269f7b2c287595.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Olga"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/b6c642f487f9b42a72a3.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/514ef575e43fa383f2c0.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Mr. Perez"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/35e0c9ad16505eca1f83.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/3b75d17ba440445688f8.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Olga"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/0c471517fad98a05e98e.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/7a74e21bec3748591698.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Olga"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/e4c09c46e175956f7766.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Mr. Perez"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/00952256293103ee775c.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/bc745e2501d64c205c49.mp3","turn":12,"speaker":"Olga"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/fb540a7482dce046eab6.mp3","turn":13,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/7cf26139f4a674df2fe5.mp3","turn":14,"speaker":"Mr. Perez"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/cf9535b52a3c33825b1a.mp3","turn":15,"speaker":"Olga"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/d71b296722ae8d9f4d0b.mp3","turn":16,"speaker":"Mr. Perez"}],"Narrator: A long time ago, a family of goats lived on East Mountain. Two of the brothers, black goat and brown goat, always fought about who was the best in the family. They were very stubborn. They never said sorry or I'm wrong. One day they were on a small patch of the greenest grass on East Mountain. It was only enough for one goat.\n\nBrown Goat: Brown goat said, I'm the oldest brother in the family, so I should eat the grass.\n\nBlack Goat: Black goat said, I'm the smartest brother in the family, so I should eat the grass.\n\nNarrator: They pushed each other with their horns. They pushed with the same force, so they didn't move forward or backward. They pushed for a long time, and then they both got tired and fell down. Black goat was angry, so he moved to West Mountain. There was a very narrow bridge between East Mountain and West Mountain. Every day, brown goat crossed it to drink from the coldest water in the pond on West Mountain. Every day, black goat crossed it to eat the juiciest grass on East Mountain. Brown goat always crossed early, and black goat always crossed late. One day, brown goat got up late, so both goats were on the bridge at the same time.\n\nBrown Goat: Brown goat said, go back. I'm the oldest, so I should cross first.\n\nBlack Goat: Black goat said, you go back. I'm the smartest, so I should cross first.\n\nNarrator: They pushed each other with their horns. They pushed with the same force, so they didn't move forward or backward. They pushed for a long time, and then they both got tired and fell into the river below the bridge. The goats swam to the riverbank. Then they slowly walked home to their mountains. They were angry, tired, wet, cold, and hungry. And that's what happens to stubborn little goats.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/67fbc4828b05f18386dd.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/20ca3189cfa1d166dbf3.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Brown Goat"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/3fa8edf105f3025edf93.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Black Goat"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/1a07bcaecd9ef0c21268.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/e0bed268a0b0b3823a71.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Brown Goat"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/454037bef9cbe026ae7d.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Black Goat"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/ab6b62ddd5a88106a5c8.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Narrator"}],"Narrator: Maki woke up early. Her room was quiet. Everyone was sleeping, even her little sister, Akiko, in the bed next to hers. What could she do?\n\nMaki: I know, she thought, I can do origami.\n\nNarrator: On the table was some colored paper. Maki got out of bed quietly. The paper was shiny, and there were a lot of colors. Maki folded a red square, bending the paper in the middle and at the edges. She worked until it was done. Suddenly, it was a crane. The crane looked lonely, so she made another, this time a blue one. Soon, she had a whole row of origami cranes.\n\nMaki: Would you like some friends? Maki asked the cranes.\n\nCranes: Oh, yes, said the cranes.\n\nMaki: You can speak? Maki laughed.\n\nCranes: Of course, you're in our origami world now.\n\nNarrator: So Maki picked up more paper. She made an orange seal. Seals like to play, Maki knew. So she made him a purple ball.\n\nSeal: Thanks, said the seal, and he rolled the ball back to her.\n\nNarrator: They played and played until Maki had another idea. With blue paper, Maki made water, crumpling it to make waves. Maki dived into the water and swam happily with the cranes and seal. A green fish jumped through the air, but something was missing. Maki remembered her sister, Akiko. She missed her and wanted to see her. Maki saw a sailboat. The boat came near and Maki heard a voice.\n\nAkiko: All aboard, the voice said.\n\nNarrator: Maki looked up, it was her sister's voice. Akiko was awake and looking for her in the origami world. She climbed into the sailboat.\n\nMaki: Hello, Akiko, she said.\n\nNarrator: Her new friends looked at her from the water, smiling. In Maki's hands was one last piece of paper, it was golden. Maki folded it, threw it high into the air, and made a big round sun.":[{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/1c8bcfc355d238b96f96.mp3","turn":0,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/03f6e285ec2e52da0e1e.mp3","turn":1,"speaker":"Maki"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/fffad40b87b0ce0e191b.mp3","turn":2,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/f55694d88d95a75eecde.mp3","turn":3,"speaker":"Maki"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/59da354411acde36559f.mp3","turn":4,"speaker":"Cranes"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/13bd6c0cdba98a482a9a.mp3","turn":5,"speaker":"Maki"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/164ca2eda533f56f0c68.mp3","turn":6,"speaker":"Cranes"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/a446bd6ff5b9c183954f.mp3","turn":7,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/f8cf8016d044d22f84d4.mp3","turn":8,"speaker":"Seal"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/d0f70eb05f0ef62371ed.mp3","turn":9,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/96543cc3fd6284cb410f.mp3","turn":10,"speaker":"Akiko"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/8cad191dd0131171b136.mp3","turn":11,"speaker":"Narrator"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/fce2d8a5590b5620478b.mp3","turn":12,"speaker":"Maki"},{"src":"../game-kit/adventures/dialogue-audio/eef885679712513eae21.mp3","turn":13,"speaker":"Narrator"}]}}